This is from mk_knox_portal():

if (! (u.uz.dnum == oracle_level.dnum	    /* in main dungeon */
	&& !at_dgn_entrance("The Quest")    /* but not Quest's entry */
	&& (u_depth = depth(&u.uz)) > 10    /* beneath 10 */
	&& u_depth < depth(&medusa_level))) /* and above Medusa */
	    return;

Four clauses arrangend so that first one that is FALSE makes the 
function return and no Ludios portal is made. Read from the top:

u.uz.dnum == oracle_level.dnum
FALSE if not in the same dungean that oracle level is => return.

!at_dgn_entrance("The Quest")
FALSE if on the same level as quest entrance => return.

(u_depth = depth(&u.uz)) > 10
FALSE if the level you are is lower than 11.

u_depth < depth(&medusa_level)

FALSE if the level you are is lower than the Medusa level.

Level that has a portal never leaves bones, so Ludios portal is never on 
a bones level.

